{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ConformalGuard: three follow-up measurements (Kaggle, about 2 to 2.5 hours of GPU session)\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Measurement | Runs on |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| A | **Judges on the multi-agent sessions** at the same per-session false-block budget as the trained scorers: violating steps blocked, latency per decision, cost per thousand decisions. Judges: Claude, DeepSeek (through OpenRouter), and two open-weight models run locally | APIs in the background; GPU for the two local models |\n",
    "| B | **More recent open-weight judges on R-Judge** under the same calibration protocol as Qwen2.5-7B: a newer model of similar size run locally, and DeepSeek through OpenRouter | GPU; API in the background |\n",
    "| C | **Closed loop**: the same simulated workspaces run without and with the guard in the loop; task success, tasks that still succeed after a block, violations prevented, false interruptions | Claude API in the background (CPU) |\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything that only calls an API runs in the background, so the GPU is busy only with the local judges.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Add-ons \u2192 Secrets: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, both attached to this notebook. Never paste a key into a cell.\n",
    "2. **Trial (15 to 20 minutes, no GPU quota).** Accelerator **None**, Internet **on**, `TRIAL = True`, **Run All**. Then check four things in the output:\n",
    "   - the OpenRouter check prints `OK: ... answered` (if it prints `FAILED`, DeepSeek is skipped: fix the key in Secrets, or the model id in the first cell, and run again);\n",
    "   - the tokenizer check for `NEW_LOCAL_MODEL` prints a prompt tail and two lists of token ids;\n",
    "   - both judge runs end with \"0 without a score\" or close to it;\n",
    "   - the closed-loop report prints a table.\n",
    "3. **Full run.** `TRIAL = False`, Accelerator **GPU T4 x2**, **Save Version \u2192 Save & Run All (Commit)**. When it finishes, open the saved version \u2192 Output \u2192 download `followup_results.zip`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Time.** Expected about 2 to 2.5 hours of GPU session for the full run (an estimate, not timed): about 30 minutes for the newer local model on R-Judge and 40 to 55 minutes for each of the two local models on the sessions, with the API work finishing in parallel. The run stops waiting at `DEADLINE_HOURS` and packs what it has.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Cost (rough).** Claude: about 15 USD for the judge on 300 sessions and about 45 USD for the closed loop on 200 workspaces (0.10 USD per session measured in the trial). DeepSeek through OpenRouter: about 6,100 short requests; see its price on OpenRouter. Lower `JUDGE_SESSIONS` or `CLOSED_LOOP_N` to spend less."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TRIAL = True                 # True: 15-20 minute check, no GPU. False: the full run (use Save & Run All).\n",
    "DEADLINE_HOURS = 4.3         # the full run stops waiting for background work after this many hours\n",
    "\n",
    "CLAUDE_MODEL = \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n",
    "CLAUDE_BACKUP = \"claude-opus-4-8\"       # agents only: used if the provider declines CLAUDE_MODEL's requests\n",
    "JUDGE_EFFORT = \"low\"\n",
    "JUDGE_SESSIONS = 300         # sessions scored by the API judges\n",
    "LOCAL_JUDGE_SESSIONS = 200   # sessions scored by the local judges (a subset of the same sample; this is the GPU time)\n",
    "\n",
    "OPENROUTER_MODEL = \"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2\"   # must be one of the ids the trial lists; \"\" skips DeepSeek\n",
    "OPENROUTER_URL = \"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\"\n",
    "\n",
    "OLD_LOCAL_MODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\"\n",
    "NEW_LOCAL_MODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen3-8B\"       # a more recent open-weight model of similar size; \"\" skips it\n",
    "NEW_LOCAL_CHAT_KWARGS = '{\"enable_thinking\": false}'   # extra chat-template arguments for NEW_LOCAL_MODEL ('' for none)\n",
    "\n",
    "CLOSED_LOOP_N = 200          # workspaces; each is run once without and once with the guard\n",
    "ALPHA = 0.10                 # the guard's per-session false-block budget in the closed loop\n",
    "WORKERS = 12\n",
    "\n",
    "# USD per million tokens, for the cost column only. Check the providers' price pages and edit. \"\" leaves the column empty.\n",
    "CLAUDE_PRICES = \"4,20,0.2,5\"     # input, output, cache read, cache write\n",
    "OPENROUTER_PRICES = \"\"           # input, output\n",
    "\n",
    "import os, signal, subprocess, time\n",
    "T0 = time.time()\n",
    "os.makedirs(\"/kaggle/temp\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.chdir(\"/kaggle/temp\")\n",
    "os.environ[\"PYTHONUNBUFFERED\"] = \"1\"\n",
    "FAILED = []\n",
    "def sh(cmd):\n",
    "    print(\"$\", cmd, flush=True)\n",
    "    get_ipython().system(cmd)\n",
    "    code = get_ipython().user_ns.get(\"_exit_code\", 0)\n",
    "    if code:\n",
    "        FAILED.append(cmd)\n",
    "        print(f\"!! exit code {code}: this command failed; later stages still run\", flush=True)\n",
    "    return code\n",
    "BRANCH = \"claude/implement-conformalguard-UGndd\"\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(\"/kaggle/temp/CV\"):\n",
    "    sh(f\"git clone -q --depth 1 -b {BRANCH} https://example.org/anonymous")\n",
    "    sh(\"git clone -q --depth 1 https://github.com/Lordog/R-Judge.git\")\n",
    "    sh(\"pip -q install sentence-transformers scikit-learn pytest accelerate anthropic openai\")\n",
    "else:                                    # a session that was used before: bring the code up to date\n",
    "    sh(f\"cd /kaggle/temp/CV && git fetch -q --depth 1 origin {BRANCH} && git reset -q --hard FETCH_HEAD\")\n",
    "os.chdir(\"/kaggle/temp/CV/ConformalGuard\")\n",
    "sh(\"git log --oneline -1\")\n",
    "assert os.path.exists(\"scripts/openai_ping.py\"), \"the code in this session is out of date: restart the session (Run \u2192 Restart & clear outputs, or a new session) and run again\"\n",
    "RJ = \"../../R-Judge\"\n",
    "RUNS = \"runs_trial\" if TRIAL else \"runs\"\n",
    "ZIP = \"/kaggle/working/\" + (\"followup_TRIAL.zip\" if TRIAL else \"followup_results.zip\")\n",
    "SESSIONS = \"results/mas_kaggle_v2/claude_sessions.jsonl.gz results/mas_kaggle_v2/openai_sessions.jsonl.gz\"\n",
    "os.makedirs(f\"{RUNS}/logs\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "def pack():\n",
    "    sh(f\"cd /kaggle/temp/CV/ConformalGuard && zip -qr {ZIP} {RUNS} -x '*/cache/*' '*.pt' && ls -la {ZIP}\")\n",
    "def hours():\n",
    "    return (time.time() - T0) / 3600\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "HAVE_GPU = torch.cuda.is_available()\n",
    "print(\"GPU:\", \"yes\" if HAVE_GPU else \"no (the two local judges are skipped; everything else runs)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# API keys come from Kaggle Secrets and are only placed in this process's environment.\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n",
    "    _secrets = UserSecretsClient()\n",
    "    for _k in (\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\", \"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\"):\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            os.environ[_k] = _secrets.get_secret(_k)\n",
    "            print(_k, \"loaded\")\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            print(_k, \"not set: that provider is skipped\")\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    print(\"not on Kaggle: using keys already in the environment, if any\")\n",
    "HAVE_CLAUDE = bool(os.environ.get(\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"))\n",
    "HAVE_OR = bool(os.environ.get(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\")) and bool(OPENROUTER_MODEL)\n",
    "sh(\"python -m pytest tests/test_mas.py tests/test_mas_followup.py -q\")\n",
    "if HAVE_OR:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nOpenRouter key and model check ({OPENROUTER_MODEL}): one tiny request\")\n",
    "    if sh(f\"python scripts/openai_ping.py --base-url {OPENROUTER_URL} --api-key-env OPENROUTER_API_KEY --model {OPENROUTER_MODEL}\"):\n",
    "        HAVE_OR = False\n",
    "        FAILED.pop()\n",
    "        print(\"!! DeepSeek is SKIPPED in this run: the line starting with FAILED above gives the reason \"\n",
    "              \"(a rejected key, or a model id the service does not know). Fix it and run again to include DeepSeek.\")\n",
    "        print(\"   DeepSeek ids listed by the service:\")\n",
    "        sh(f\"python scripts/openai_list_models.py --base-url {OPENROUTER_URL} --api-key-env OPENROUTER_API_KEY --filter deepseek\")\n",
    "if TRIAL and NEW_LOCAL_MODEL:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nTokenizer check for {NEW_LOCAL_MODEL} (downloads the tokenizer only):\")\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import json, sys\n",
    "        sys.path.insert(0, \"scripts\")\n",
    "        import rjudge_judge_local as RL\n",
    "        from transformers import AutoTokenizer\n",
    "        tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(NEW_LOCAL_MODEL)\n",
    "        ids = RL.chat_ids(tok, [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a monitor.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Answer with one letter only: A or B.\"}],\n",
    "                          json.loads(NEW_LOCAL_CHAT_KWARGS) if NEW_LOCAL_CHAT_KWARGS else None)\n",
    "        print(\"prompt tail:\", repr(tok.decode(ids[0][-30:])))\n",
    "        print(\"token ids for A and B:\", RL.letter_ids(tok))\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print(f\"!! {type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:300]}\\n   Put another open-weight chat model in NEW_LOCAL_MODEL, or '' to skip it.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Background work: API judges and the closed loop\n",
    "\n",
    "Three chains, started here and left running while the GPU cells below work. In the trial they run in the foreground on a few items. Logs are in `runs/logs/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **claude_judge**: Claude scores every proposed action of the sampled sessions (A).\n",
    "- **openrouter**: DeepSeek scores R-Judge step by step (B), then the sampled sessions (A).\n",
    "- **closed_loop**: trains the guard on CPU, then runs new workspaces without and with it (C)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "NJ = 3 if TRIAL else JUDGE_SESSIONS\n",
    "P = 1 if TRIAL else 2              # the second pass retries calls and sessions that failed\n",
    "CHAINS = {}\n",
    "if HAVE_CLAUDE:\n",
    "    CHAINS[\"claude_judge\"] = [f\"python scripts/mas_judge_claude.py --sessions {SESSIONS} --n-sessions {NJ} --model {CLAUDE_MODEL} \"\n",
    "                              f\"--effort {JUDGE_EFFORT} --out {RUNS}/mas_judge_claude\"] * P\n",
    "    n, epochs = (3, 6) if TRIAL else (CLOSED_LOOP_N, 40)\n",
    "    backup = f\"--backup-model {CLAUDE_BACKUP} \" if CLAUDE_BACKUP else \"\"\n",
    "    CHAINS[\"closed_loop\"] = [f\"python scripts/mas_closed_loop_claude.py --train-sessions {SESSIONS} --n {n} --alpha {ALPHA} --epochs {epochs} \"\n",
    "                             f\"--model {CLAUDE_MODEL} {backup}--workers {WORKERS} --device cpu --out {RUNS}/closed_loop\"] * P\n",
    "if HAVE_OR:\n",
    "    lim = \"--limit 5\" if TRIAL else \"\"\n",
    "    CHAINS[\"openrouter\"] = ([f\"python scripts/rjudge_judge_openai.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --model {OPENROUTER_MODEL} --mode causal {lim} \"\n",
    "                             f\"--base-url {OPENROUTER_URL} --api-key-env OPENROUTER_API_KEY --out {RUNS}/guard_deepseek_causal\"] * P\n",
    "                            + [f\"python scripts/mas_judge_openai.py --sessions {SESSIONS} --n-sessions {NJ} --model {OPENROUTER_MODEL} \"\n",
    "                               f\"--base-url {OPENROUTER_URL} --api-key-env OPENROUTER_API_KEY --out {RUNS}/mas_judge_deepseek\"] * P)\n",
    "JOBS = {}\n",
    "for name, cmds in CHAINS.items():\n",
    "    if TRIAL:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n===== {name} =====\"); [sh(c) for c in cmds]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        log = open(f\"{RUNS}/logs/{name}.log\", \"w\")\n",
    "        JOBS[name] = subprocess.Popen([\"bash\", \"-c\", \" ; \".join(cmds)], stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, start_new_session=True)\n",
    "        print(f\"started {name} in the background; log: {RUNS}/logs/{name}.log\")\n",
    "def status():\n",
    "    for name, p in JOBS.items():\n",
    "        print(f\"[{hours():.1f} h] {name}: {'running' if p.poll() is None else 'finished'};\", end=\" \", flush=True)\n",
    "        sh(f\"tail -n 1 {RUNS}/logs/{name}.log\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## B (GPU). A more recent open-weight model of similar size on R-Judge\n",
    "\n",
    "Same prompt, one-letter scoring and calibration as for Qwen2.5-7B, whose scores from the earlier run are in the repository. Skipped in the trial and without a GPU."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if TRIAL or not HAVE_GPU or not NEW_LOCAL_MODEL:\n",
    "    print(\"skipped (trial, no GPU, or NEW_LOCAL_MODEL is empty)\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    kw = f\"--chat-kwargs '{NEW_LOCAL_CHAT_KWARGS}'\" if NEW_LOCAL_CHAT_KWARGS else \"\"\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/rjudge_judge_local.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --model {NEW_LOCAL_MODEL} --mode causal {kw} --out {RUNS}/guard_local_new_causal\")\n",
    "    pack(); status()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## A (GPU). The two local open-weight judges on the sessions\n",
    "\n",
    "A subset of the sessions the API judges score. Skipped in the trial and without a GPU."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if TRIAL or not HAVE_GPU:\n",
    "    print(\"skipped (trial or no GPU)\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    if NEW_LOCAL_MODEL:          # the newer model first: its weights are already downloaded\n",
    "        kw = f\"--chat-kwargs '{NEW_LOCAL_CHAT_KWARGS}'\" if NEW_LOCAL_CHAT_KWARGS else \"\"\n",
    "        sh(f\"python scripts/mas_judge_local.py --sessions {SESSIONS} --n-sessions {LOCAL_JUDGE_SESSIONS} --model {NEW_LOCAL_MODEL} {kw} --out {RUNS}/mas_judge_new\")\n",
    "        pack(); status()\n",
    "    if hours() < DEADLINE_HOURS - 0.75:\n",
    "        sh(f\"python scripts/mas_judge_local.py --sessions {SESSIONS} --n-sessions {LOCAL_JUDGE_SESSIONS} --model {OLD_LOCAL_MODEL} --out {RUNS}/mas_judge_qwen25\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"skipped the older local model: too close to DEADLINE_HOURS\")\n",
    "    pack(); status()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Wait for the background work, then write the three reports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "while any(p.poll() is None for p in JOBS.values()) and hours() < DEADLINE_HOURS:\n",
    "    time.sleep(120); status()\n",
    "for name, p in JOBS.items():\n",
    "    if p.poll() is None:\n",
    "        os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGTERM)\n",
    "        print(f\"{name} stopped at the deadline; what it wrote so far is kept and used\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n--- log of {name}\"); sh(f\"grep -v 'steps scored\\\\|sessions written\\\\|^  [0-9]*/' {RUNS}/logs/{name}.log | tail -n 25\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex = lambda d: os.path.exists(f\"{RUNS}/{d}/scores.jsonl\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n===== B. Open-weight judges on R-Judge =====\")\n",
    "specs = \"qwen25_causal=results/kaggle_extra/guard_scores/local_causal.jsonl\"\n",
    "specs += f\" new_local_causal={RUNS}/guard_local_new_causal/scores.jsonl\" if ex(\"guard_local_new_causal\") else \"\"\n",
    "specs += f\" deepseek_causal={RUNS}/guard_deepseek_causal/scores.jsonl\" if ex(\"guard_deepseek_causal\") else \"\"\n",
    "if TRIAL:\n",
    "    print(\"TRIAL: skipped (five records are too few to calibrate on)\")\n",
    "elif \"=runs\" in specs:\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/rjudge_guard_eval.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --scores {specs} --reps 1000 --out {RUNS}/rjudge_openweight_eval\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n===== A. Judges on the multi-agent sessions =====\")\n",
    "specs = \" \".join(f\"{n}={RUNS}/{d}/scores.jsonl\" for n, d in ((\"claude\", \"mas_judge_claude\"), (\"deepseek\", \"mas_judge_deepseek\"),\n",
    "                                                             (\"new_local\", \"mas_judge_new\"), (\"qwen25\", \"mas_judge_qwen25\")) if ex(d))\n",
    "prices = (f\" claude={CLAUDE_PRICES}\" if CLAUDE_PRICES else \"\") + (f\" deepseek={OPENROUTER_PRICES}\" if OPENROUTER_PRICES else \"\")\n",
    "if specs:\n",
    "    if TRIAL:\n",
    "        print(\"TRIAL: three sessions are too few to calibrate on; the evaluator is run only to check that it works.\")\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/mas_guard_eval.py --sessions {SESSIONS} --scores {specs}\" + (f\" --prices{prices}\" if prices else \"\")\n",
    "       + f\" --trained results/mas_kaggle_v2/results.json --reps {20 if TRIAL else 500} --out {RUNS}/mas_guard_eval\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n===== C. Closed loop =====\")\n",
    "if os.path.exists(f\"{RUNS}/closed_loop/guard.pt\"):\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/mas_closed_loop_claude.py --train-sessions {SESSIONS} --report-only --out {RUNS}/closed_loop\")\n",
    "pack()\n",
    "if FAILED:\n",
    "    print(f\"{len(FAILED)} command(s) FAILED; scroll up to their output:\")\n",
    "    for c in FAILED:\n",
    "        print(\"  \", c)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"every foreground command exited normally (check the background logs above for errors)\")\n",
    "print(f\"finished after {hours():.2f} h. \" + (\"This was a TRIAL: its outputs are smoke runs, not results. If the four checks in the first cell pass, set TRIAL = False.\"\n",
    "                                             if TRIAL else \"Download followup_results.zip from this version's Output tab.\"))"
   ]
  }
 ],
